    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "header",
            "block_content": " Part 6 Provisions relating to governing rules of superannuation entities ",
            "block_bbox": [
                147,
                0,
                847,
                24
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Section 55A ",
            "block_bbox": [
                151,
                90,
                303,
                112
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "sections 52 to 53 and prescribed under section 54A that apply to the defendant in relation to each act, or failure to act, that resulted in the loss or damage.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                294,
                155,
                1000,
                235
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(6) It is a defence to an action for loss or damage suffered by a person.as a result of the management of any reserves by a trustee of a superannuation entity if the defendant establishes that the defendant has complied with all of the covenants referred to in sections 52 to 53 and prescribed under section 54A that apply to the defendant in relation to each act, or failure to act, that resulted in the loss or damage.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                255,
                259,
                1011,
                452
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(7) Subsections (5) and (6) apply to an action for loss or damage,whether brought under subsection (3) or otherwise.",
            "block_bbox": [
                256,
                475,
                963,
                530
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "55A Rules about cashing benefits after death of members ",
            "block_bbox": [
                161,
                565,
                885,
                591
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) The governing rules of a regulated superannuation fund must not permit a fund member's benefits to be cashed after the member's.death otherwise than in accordance with standards prescribed for the purposes of section 31.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                252,
                616,
                1009,
                729
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) If the governing rules of a fund are inconsistent with subsection (1):",
            "block_bbox": [
                251,
                754,
                873,
                807
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(a) subsection (1) prevails; and ",
            "block_bbox": [
                315,
                815,
                667,
                840
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(b) the governing rules are invalid, to the extent of the inconsistency.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                313,
                849,
                915,
                901
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "55B Governing rules do not prevent giving effect to certain elections ",
            "block_bbox": [
                159,
                938,
                1031,
                963
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A provision in the governing rules of a regulated superannuation fund is void to the extent that it would prevent a trustee or trustees of the fund from giving effect to:",
            "block_bbox": [
                296,
                987,
                1027,
                1068
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(a) an election made in accordance with section 29SAA (election to transfer accrued default amounts to a MySuper product);or \n",
            "block_bbox": [
                315,
                1077,
                1034,
                1156
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "number",
            "block_content": "234",
            "block_bbox": [
                161,
                1304,
